      "source": [
        "# Time Series Forecasting: NeuralForecast, Prophet & Hierarchical — Module 4 Specialization\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning Objectives\n",
        "- **NeuralForecast**: Deep learning models (N-HiTS, N-BEATS, TFT) for scalable forecasting\n",
        "- **Prophet**: Facebook's additive trend + seasonality model with holiday effects\n",
        "- **Hierarchical Forecasting**: Bottom-up, top-down, and optimal reconciliation (MinTrace)\n",
        "- **Exogenous Variables**: Covariates, interventions, and causal impact\n",
        "- **Evaluation**: MAE, MASE, RMSE, CRPS for probabilistic forecasts\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters\n",
        "Time series forecasting is critical for demand planning, inventory optimization, capacity planning, and financial modeling. ML Architects must choose between statistical (Prophet), deep learning (NeuralForecast), and hierarchical approaches based on data volume, interpretability needs, and hierarchy structure. This notebook implements all three with real training and evaluation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install required packages\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "!{sys.executable} -m pip install neuralforecast prophet pandas numpy matplotlib scikit-learn -q 2>/dev/null || true"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate synthetic time series data with trend, seasonality, and exogenous variables\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "n = 730  # 2 years of daily data\n",
        "dates = pd.date_range('2022-01-01', periods=n, freq='D')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Base components\n",
        "trend = 0.02 * np.arange(n)\n",
        "yearly_seasonality = 10 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.arange(n) / 365.25)\n",
        "weekly_seasonality = 5 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.arange(n) / 7)\n",
        "noise = np.random.normal(0, 2, n)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Exogenous variable (e.g., marketing spend, temperature)\n",
        "exog = 3 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.arange(n) / 30) + np.random.normal(0, 1, n)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Target: combine all components\n",
        "y = 100 + trend + yearly_seasonality + weekly_seasonality + 0.5 * exog + noise\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create DataFrame in NeuralForecast format\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'unique_id': 'series_1',\n",
        "    'ds': dates,\n",
        "    'y': y,\n",
        "    'exog_1': exog\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "# Split train/test (last 90 days for test)\n",
        "test_horizon = 90\n",
        "train_df = df.iloc[:-test_horizon].copy()\n",
        "test_df = df.iloc[-test_horizon:].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Train: {len(train_df)} samples, Test: {len(test_df)} samples\")\n",
        "print(f\"Date range: {df['ds'].min()} to {df['ds'].max()}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(12, 8))\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df['ds'], df['y'], label='Target (y)', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[0].set_title('Synthetic Time Series with Trend, Seasonality & Exogenous')\n",
        "axes[0].legend()\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df['ds'], df['exog_1'], label='Exogenous Variable', color='orange', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[1].set_title('Exogenous Covariate')\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Prophet: Interpretable Trend + Seasonality Decomposition\n",
        "\n",
        "Prophet uses an additive model: `y(t) = g(t) + s(t) + h(t) + ε(t)` where:\n",
        "- `g(t)`: piecewise linear or logistic growth trend\n",
        "- `s(t)`: yearly/weekly/daily seasonality (Fourier series)\n",
        "- `h(t)`: holiday effects\n",
        "- `ε(t)`: error term\n",
        "\n",
        "Key advantage: **interpretable components** and built-in handling of missing data, outliers, and holidays."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from prophet import Prophet\n",
        "\n",
        "# Prepare data for Prophet (requires 'ds' and 'y' columns)\n",
        "prophet_train = train_df[['ds', 'y']].rename(columns={'ds': 'ds', 'y': 'y'}).copy()\n",
        "prophet_train['exog_1'] = train_df['exog_1'].values\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize Prophet with exogenous regressor\n",
        "model_prophet = Prophet(\n",
        "    yearly_seasonality=True,\n",
        "    weekly_seasonality=True,\n",
        "    daily_seasonality=False,\n",
        "    seasonality_mode='additive',\n",
        "    changepoint_prior_scale=0.05,\n",
        "    interval_width=0.95\n",
        ")\n",
        "model_prophet.add_regressor('exog_1')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit\n",
        "model_prophet.fit(prophet_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create future dataframe with exogenous values\n",
        "future = model_prophet.make_future_dataframe(periods=test_horizon, freq='D')\n",
        "future['exog_1'] = df['exog_1'].values[-len(future):]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Predict\n",
        "forecast = model_prophet.predict(future)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Extract test predictions\n",
        "prophet_pred = forecast.iloc[-test_horizon:][['ds', 'yhat', 'yhat_lower', 'yhat_upper']].copy()\n",
        "prophet_pred.columns = ['ds', 'prophet', 'prophet_lower', 'prophet_upper']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot components\n",
        "fig = model_prophet.plot_components(forecast)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Prophet training complete. Components plotted above.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. NeuralForecast: Deep Learning Models for Scalable Forecasting\n",
        "\n",
        "NeuralForecast provides SOTA deep learning models:\n",
        "- **N-BEATS**: Deep backward/forward residual links, interpretable trend/seasonality\n",
        "- **N-HiTS**: Hierarchical interpolation with multi-rate sampling, faster training\n",
        "- **TFT (Temporal Fusion Transformer)**: Attention-based, handles static/known/observed covariates\n",
        "- **PatchTST**: Patch-based Transformer for long sequences\n",
        "- **TiDE**: MLP-based, extremely fast training\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll demonstrate N-HiTS (fast, accurate) and TFT (handles exogenous variables natively)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from neuralforecast import NeuralForecast\n",
        "from neuralforecast.models import NHITS, TFT\n",
        "from neuralforecast.losses.pytorch import MQLoss, DistributionLoss\n",
        "\n",
        "# Prepare data in NeuralForecast format (already done above)\n",
        "# train_df has columns: unique_id, ds, y, exog_1\n",
        "\n",
        "# N-HiTS: Hierarchical interpolation, multi-rate sampling\n",
        "nhits = NHITS(\n",
        "    h=test_horizon,\n",
        "    input_size=2 * test_horizon,  # lookback window\n",
        "    n_blocks=3,\n",
        "    n_layers=2,\n",
        "    mlp_units=[64, 64],\n",
        "    n_pool_kernel_size=[2, 2, 1],\n",
        "    n_freq_downsample=[168, 24, 1],  # weekly, daily, hourly rates\n",
        "    learning_rate=1e-3,\n",
        "    max_steps=200,\n",
        "    val_check_steps=50,\n",
        "    random_seed=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# TFT: Temporal Fusion Transformer with attention\n",
        "tft = TFT(\n",
        "    h=test_horizon,\n",
        "    input_size=2 * test_horizon,\n",
        "    hidden_size=64,\n",
        "    n_head=4,\n",
        "    learning_rate=1e-3,\n",
        "    max_steps=200,\n",
        "    val_check_steps=50,\n",
        "    random_seed=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize NeuralForecast\n",
        "nf = NeuralForecast(\n",
        "    models=[nhits, tft],\n",
        "    freq='D'\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit\n",
        "nf.fit(df=train_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Predict\n",
        "nf_forecast = nf.predict()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Merge predictions\n",
        "nf_forecast = nf_forecast.reset_index()\n",
        "print(f\"NeuralForecast predictions shape: {nf_forecast.shape}\")\n",
        "print(nf_forecast.head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Evaluation: Point & Probabilistic Metrics\n",
        "\n",
        "Compare Prophet, N-HiTS, and TFT on test set using multiple metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error\n",
        "\n",
        "def mase(y_true, y_pred, y_train, seasonality=7):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Mean Absolute Scaled Error\"\"\"\n",
        "    mae = mean_absolute_error(y_true, y_pred)\n",
        "    # Naive seasonal forecast error\n",
        "    naive_errors = np.abs(y_train[seasonality:] - y_train[:-seasonality])\n",
        "    scale = np.mean(naive_errors)\n",
        "    return mae / scale if scale > 0 else np.inf\n",
        "\n",
        "def crps_gaussian(y_true, mu, sigma):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Continuous Ranked Probability Score for Gaussian predictive distribution\"\"\"\n",
        "    from scipy.stats import norm\n",
        "    z = (y_true - mu) / sigma\n",
        "    return sigma * (z * (2 * norm.cdf(z) - 1) + 2 * norm.pdf(z) - 1/np.sqrt(np.pi))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ground truth\n",
        "y_true = test_df['y'].values\n",
        "\n",
        "# Prophet predictions\n",
        "prophet_y = prophet_pred['prophet'].values\n",
        "prophet_lower = prophet_pred['prophet_lower'].values\n",
        "prophet_upper = prophet_pred['prophet_upper'].values\n",
        "prophet_sigma = (prophet_upper - prophet_lower) / (2 * 1.96)  # 95% interval\n",
        "\n",
        "# NeuralForecast predictions\n",
        "nhits_y = nf_forecast[nf_forecast['unique_id'] == 'series_1']['NHITS'].values\n",
        "tft_y = nf_forecast[nf_forecast['unique_id'] == 'series_1']['TFT'].values\n",
        "\n",
        "# Metrics\n",
        "models = {\n",
        "    'Prophet': prophet_y,\n",
        "    'N-HiTS': nhits_y,\n",
        "    'TFT': tft_y\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "y_train = train_df['y'].values\n",
        "\n",
        "results = []\n",
        "for name, y_pred in models.items():\n",
        "    mae = mean_absolute_error(y_true, y_pred)\n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred))\n",
        "    mase_val = mase(y_true, y_pred, y_train)\n",
        "    results.append({'Model': name, 'MAE': mae, 'RMSE': rmse, 'MASE': mase_val})\n",
        "    print(f\"{name}: MAE={mae:.3f}, RMSE={rmse:.3f}, MASE={mase_val:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
        "print(\"\\nEvaluation Summary:\")\n",
        "print(results_df.to_string(index=False))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Visualization: Forecast Comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Plot forecasts vs actual\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(14, 12), sharex=True)\n",
