        "## 10. Summary & Model Selection Guide\n",
        "\n",
        "| Scenario | Recommended Approach | Reason |\n",
        "|----------|---------------------|--------|\n",
        "| Interpretable, few series, holidays | **Prophet** | Decomposable, handles missing data, business-friendly |\n",
        "| Many series (1000+), high accuracy | **N-HiTS / N-BEATS** | Fast training, hierarchical, multi-rate sampling |\n",
        "| Complex covariates, attention needed | **TFT / PatchTST** | Handles static/known/observed inputs, interpretability |\n",
        "| Hierarchical (product→region→total) | **MinTrace reconciliation** | Coherent forecasts, optimal combination |\n",
        "| Causal intervention analysis | **Prophet + regressors** | Explicit coefficient estimation |\n",
        "| Long horizon, high frequency | **PatchTST / TiDE** | Patch-based attention, MLP efficiency |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key Takeaway**: ML Architects should match model complexity to problem structure. Start simple (Prophet), scale to deep learning (NeuralForecast) when data volume and accuracy demands justify it. Always reconcile hierarchical forecasts for coherence."
      ]
